我们发现了他是和谁一起去的。

25
00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

26
00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.190
Yes, we do.
没错，我们发现了。

27
00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:13.290
Jan.
是简。

28
00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.450
Scandalous office romance.
办公室里的绯闻恋情。

29
00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:28.470
Well, despite Jan's insistence that Michael keep their vacation a secret, Michael accidentally circulates an intimate photo of them to the entire office and beyond.
尽管简坚持要求迈克尔对他们的假期保密，但迈克尔还是不小心把一张他们的亲密照片发给了整个办公室，甚至传到了外面。

30
00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:36.810
So, he and Dwight are going to spend this episode trying to retrieve and delete the photo while Michael awaits Jan's arrival in Scranton.
所以，他和德怀特这一集都在忙着试图找回并删除那张照片，同时迈克尔还在等待简抵达斯克兰顿。

31
00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:45.190
Meanwhile, Angela has to throw together a last-minute luau, and Pam gives Jim advice that helps his relationship with Karen.
与此同时，安吉拉不得不临时筹办一场夏威夷派对，而帕姆给了吉姆一些建议，帮助了他与凯伦的关系。

32
00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:46.430
Hmm.
嗯。

33
00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:47.490
Yeah.
没错。

34
00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.570
Let's jump into fast fact number one.
让我们进入第一个速览事实。

35
00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.650
This episode was written by Justin Spitzer.
这一集是由贾斯汀·斯皮策编剧的。

36
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.350
Now, we talked a little bit about Justin before.
我们之前聊过一点关于贾斯汀的事。

37
00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:03.950
He created the show Superstore, and remember, we found out that he's the person that wrote the twin absorption line for Dwight in Grief Counseling.
他创作了《爆笑超市》，还记得吗，我们发现他在《悲伤辅导》那一集中写了德怀特关于“双胞胎吸收”的台词。

38
00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.350
Yes, that was the ginsalata deep dive, and we found that out.
没错，那是关于“金萨拉塔”的深度挖掘，我们当时发现了这一点。

39
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.310
Well, this was Justin's first full episode.
这一集是贾斯汀完整编剧的第一集。

40
00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.950
So, I reached out to him because I've kept in touch with Justin since we wrapped.
所以我联系了他，因为自从剧集结束后，我就一直和贾斯汀保持着联系。

41
00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.110
Justin's just one of my favorite people, I have to say.
我必须得说，贾斯汀是我最喜欢的人之一。

42
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.630
He is so lovely.
他真是太可爱了。

43
00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:27.890
So, I reached out to Justin, and I asked him, where did the idea for this episode come from?
所以我联系了贾斯汀，问他这一集的灵感是从哪里来的？

44
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.830
And he said it was really simple.
他说其实很简单。

45
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:41.230
Greg really wanted to explore this idea of that feeling you get when you have to come back from your vacation and go back to your work grind.
格雷格真的很想探讨那种度假结束、不得不回到枯燥工作中的感觉。

46
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.950
And that was it.
就是这样。

47
00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:46.690
That was, they built the whole story around that one theme.
他们就是围绕这个主题构建了整个故事。

48
00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:53.310
You know what I love about that is that I find the stories I like the most have such a simple premise.
你知道我喜欢这一点的原因吗？因为我发现我最喜欢的故事往往都有一个非常简单的前提。

49
00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.370
They're not heavy on premise, and I find them usually the most relatable.
它们的前提并不沉重，而且我发现它们通常最能引起共鸣。

50
00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.450
Same, same.
我也是，我也是。

51
00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.230
I feel like that's what made Halloween so great.
我觉得这就是万圣节那么棒的原因。

52
00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.430
You have to fire someone on Halloween.
你得在万圣节那天解雇某人。

53
00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:06.530
Yeah.
没错。

54
00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:08.110
That's it.
就是这样。

55
00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:08.970
That's it.
就是这样。

56
00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:09.850
That's it.
就是这样。

57
00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.010
You've just had a great vacation, and now you're faced with the reality of your life back home.
你刚度过了一个很棒的假期，现在不得不面对回到家后的现实生活。

58
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:15.350
Yes.
是的。

59
00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.910
So, then I asked Justin, what was it like being your first full script?
所以，我问了贾斯汀，第一次独立完成完整剧本是什么感觉？

60
00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:30.410
And he said he was incredibly nervous about doing a good job, and he remembers that it was normal for writers to get a full week to write their first draft.
他说他当时非常紧张，想把工作做好，他还记得编剧通常有一整周的时间来写初稿。

61
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:38.830
You would usually get sent off on a Friday, and you would have the whole next week, and it wouldn't be due until the following Monday.
通常周五会把任务派发给你，你有一整周的时间，直到下周一才交稿。

62
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.450
You'd get about nine days.
你大概有九天时间。

63
00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:52.130
So, he said that this script, though, they did not finish breaking it until Monday night, pretty late, and Greg said, I'm going to need this Friday morning.
所以他说，这次的剧本，他们直到周一晚上很晚才完成大纲，格雷格说，我周五早上就要用到它。

64
00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:52.970
Ah!
啊！

65
00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.330
So, he only had three days.
所以他只有三天时间。

66
00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:01.370
This is reminding me of when Gene and Lee had to do their first script in, like, three days.
这让我想起吉恩和李第一次写剧本时，也只用了三天左右。

67
00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:06.570
Yeah, or the time Steve had to write his script over a weekend with his in-laws visiting.
没错，还有史蒂夫那次，他在岳父母来访的周末写完了剧本。

68
00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.190
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

69
00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:08.710
Exactly.
确实。

70
00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.830
Justin said he grabbed a case of Diet Coke out of the kitchen.
贾斯汀说他从厨房拿了一箱健怡可乐。

71
00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:15.530
He said he basically lived on that for the next 72 hours.
他说接下来的72小时他基本就是靠这个活下来的。

72
00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:16.350
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

73
00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:26.530
And I guess, apparently, after Justin left to go write the script, because you could write your scripts at home, one of the other writers said to Greg, we're not behind.
我猜，显然在贾斯汀离开去写剧本后——因为你可以在家写剧本——另一位编剧对格雷格说，我们进度并不落后。

74
00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.390
Why does he have to write it so fast?
为什么非要让他写得这么快？

75
00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.770
And that Greg smiled and said, to keep the pressure up, just tighten in the screws.
格雷格笑了笑说，为了保持压力，得拧紧发条。

76
00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.710
Oh, Greg!
哦，格雷格！

77
00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:45.320
I think in retrospect, it weirdly did relieve some of the pressure of it being the very first script that he was writing,
我觉得事后看来，这反而奇怪地减轻了他作为第一次写剧本的压力，

78
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:50.680
because no one really expects a script that you write in only three days to be very good.
因为没人会指望你只花三天写出来的剧本能有多好。

79
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.320
So, he was like, well, this is what it is.
所以他想，好吧，就这样吧。

80
00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.080
