他们给了我一叠明信片，我一张接一张地举起来，我觉得这很

293
00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.940
sweet because that means Pam saves them.
贴心，因为这意味着帕姆把它们都留着。

294
00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.160
I know.
我知道。

295
00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.900
And to me, it's like you just really see who Pam is to Michael.
对我来说，这真的能让你看出帕姆对迈克尔来说意味着什么。

296
00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:19.260
You see why ultimately she's the last person he speaks to before he leaves.
你也能明白为什么最终她是他在离开前最后一个交谈的人。

297
00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:25.360
At the end of, you know, his time on the office, like he sees her as family.
在他离开《办公室》的最后时刻，他把她视为家人。

298
00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:26.900
I really think he does.
我真的觉得他是这么想的。

299
00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.860
Well, we had a fan question for this opening scene.
好吧，我们有一个关于这个开场戏的粉丝提问。

300
00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:37.600
There's that moment where Michael shakes his hair at Pam because he's gotten some little
有一个瞬间，迈克尔对着帕姆甩了甩头发，因为他弄到了一些小东西

301
00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.600
beads in his hair on his vacation.
度假时头发上编着小辫子。

302
00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.800
I'm telling you, sandals was like adult camp for Michael.
我跟你说，桑达尔斯度假村对迈克尔来说就像成人夏令营一样。

303
00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.420
I mean, he says how you go, hey, man.
我是说，他会说，嘿，伙计。

304
00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:46.800
And then everyone yells, hey, man.
然后大家都会喊，嘿，伙计。

305
00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.020
I can see him being so enthusiastic.
我能想象他有多兴奋。

306
00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.640
He's going to do everything.
他什么都会去尝试。

307
00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.800
Braid my hair.
编辫子。

308
00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.020
Learn the dances.
学跳舞。

309
00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:53.980
Learn the chants.
学口号。

310
00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.200
He's in it, Jenna.
他完全沉浸其中了，珍娜。

311
00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:56.780
He's in it.
他真的投入进去了。

312
00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:57.300
You're right.
你说得对。

313
00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:04.060
Well, we had this question from Ashley Browning, Hope Cogbill, Jess Graham, Rachel LaPointe,
嗯，我们收到了来自阿什莉·布朗宁、霍普·科格比尔、杰斯·格雷厄姆、瑞秋·拉波因特，

314
00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.780
and Teresa Rambucuela.
以及特蕾莎·兰布库埃拉的问题。

315
00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.540
They want to know whose idea was it to put the beads in the hair?
她们想知道，给头发编上小辫子是谁的主意？

316
00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.660
Were they sewn in?
它们是缝上去的吗？

317
00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:11.680
Were they glued in?
还是粘上去的？

318
00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.440
Well, Jenna, you know, we wanted to get the behind the scenes story on this braid.
嗯，珍娜，你知道，我们想了解一下这个发型背后的故事。

319
00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:21.020
So we reached out to Kim Ferry, who did our hair on the office for all the scoop.
所以我们联系了在《办公室》负责我们发型的金·费里，想打听一下内幕。

320
00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.640
And this is what she had to say.
这就是她要说的。

321
00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.780
Well, hello, lovely office ladies.
嗯，你们好，可爱的《办公室》女士们。

322
00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:28.680
Gosh darn it, I miss both of you so much.
天哪，我太想念你们俩了。

323
00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.960
Thank you for asking me these questions.
谢谢你们问我这些问题。

324
00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:38.460
As usual, if there were any hair gags, Greg Daniels would either have me paged up or he
像往常一样，如果有任何关于发型的恶搞，格雷格·丹尼尔斯要么会传呼我，要么

325
00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:43.280
would come find me and we would discuss what the look would be for whatever the actors were
会来找我，我们会讨论演员在这一集中

326
00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.680
doing in this episode.
需要什么样的造型。

327
00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.820
In this one, it was specifically Michael Scott.
在这一集里，具体是迈克尔·斯科特。

328
00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:53.820
And I know on the makeup side, he was going to be tan because they wanted him to kind of
我知道在化妆方面，他需要晒黑，因为他们想让他看起来

329
00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:56.100
have that, you know, tan glow from Jamaica.
有一种从牙买加回来后的那种晒黑的光泽感。

330
00:16:56.260 --> 00:17:00.760
But on my side, it was about having something in his hair.
但在我这边，重点是要在他的头发上弄点东西。

331
00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.020
Could it be dreaded?
是弄成脏辫吗？

332
00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.000
Could it be beaded?
还是编上珠子？

333
00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:04.480
You know, what could we do?
你知道，我们能做点什么呢？

334
00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:09.560
And in the end, I kind of liked the idea of putting beads in.
最后，我挺喜欢编珠子这个主意的。

335
00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:16.220
But I was a little nervous because his hair was only one inch on the sides in the back.
但我有点紧张，因为他侧面和后面的头发只有一英寸长。

336
00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:17.920
He had a short haircut at that time.
他当时留的是短发。

337
00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:20.840
So I wasn't sure if something would stick in there.
所以我不太确定能不能固定住。

338
00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:26.520
But I, you know, I rose to the challenge and told my team I was going to be in the trailer
但我，你知道，我迎接了这个挑战，告诉我的团队我要在化妆车里

339
00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.200
for a little bit.
待一会儿。

340
00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.120
And I did a couple of variations of it.
我做了几种不同的尝试。

341
00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.420
And I also had human hair.
我还用了真人头发。

342
00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:35.380
So you can have these actual real human hair clips.
所以你可以用这些真正的真人发片。

343
00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:39.280
And I would sew them into these little things called toupee clips.
我会把它们缝在一种叫假发夹的小东西上。

344
00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:45.840
And I ended up braiding it down probably about two inches long, two to three inches long.
最后我编了大概两英寸长，两到三英寸长。

345
00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.220
And at the very end, I had a little elastic on the bottom.
在最末端，我用了一个小橡皮筋。

346
00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:51.480
And that really held all the beads in place.
那真的把所有的珠子都固定住了。

347
00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:56.660
And I know I had done a few options for Greg with different colors.
我知道我为格雷格提供了几种不同颜色的选择。

348
00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:59.700
But in the end, he liked the red and yellow and green.
但最后，他喜欢红色、黄色和绿色的。

349
00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.240
So that's what we went with.
所以我们就选了那个。

350
00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.680
And the little clip, it just kind of like hooks into the hair.
那个小夹子，就像钩子一样钩在头发上。

351
00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.320
So it sticks really well.
所以它粘得非常牢。

352
00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:12.660
And if I just back combed it a little bit and then a little bit of hairspray and then pop
如果我把它稍微倒梳一下，再喷点发胶，然后啪地一下

353
00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:15.020
that clip in, it wasn't going anywhere.
把发夹别上去，它就纹丝不动了。

354
00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:15.920
And it didn't.
确实没动。

355
00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.260
It didn't move at all during that episode.
那一集里它一点都没动过。

356
00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:19.780
So I was very happy.
所以我非常满意。

357
00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:22.840
But that's just one of the things that I love doing.
但这只是我喜欢做的事情之一。

358
00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:26.640
When I get challenges from Greg, it was always fun to not only,
当格雷格给我出难题时，不仅能让他看到成品后感到高兴，

359
00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:33.560
make him happy after he saw it, but just to kind of really, he would enjoy it.
而且他真的会很享受这个过程，这总是很有趣。

360
00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:37.200
It made me so happy when he would smile and he'd be like, yeah, yeah, that's it.
每当他露出笑容，说“对，对，就是这样”时，我都会感到非常开心。

361
00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.120
So that is my story for this episode.
这就是我这一集的故事。

362
00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.720
And I miss you both so much.
我非常想念你们俩。

363
00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:42.820
And I'm sending you hugs.
给你们一个大大的拥抱。

364
00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:43.960
And I'm so proud of you.
我为你们感到骄傲。

365
00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.120
I love your podcaSt.
我爱你们的播客。

366
00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.800
And I can't wait to hopefully join you guys there someday.
我迫不及待地希望有一天能加入你们。

367
00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.740
All right, you guys, take care.
好了，你们多保重。

368
00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:50.720
Love you both.
爱你们俩。

369
00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:51.360
Bye.
再见。

370
00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:59.900
Love knowing that they didn't do anything to his actual hair.
很高兴知道他们没有动他原本的头发。

371
00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:02.000
She would just clip that in and out every day.
她每天只是把那个夹上去再取下来。

372
00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:03.060
Yeah.
没错。

373
00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:10.960
I remember Kim always having these heads with like different like forms of hair and wigs and braids and
我记得金总是放着这些假人头，上面有各种各样的头发、假发、辫子，

374
00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.480
like whatever she was tinkering on.
还有她正在捣鼓的各种东西。

375
00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:18.580
She had like a row of like fake hair with like different versions of things, especially for Meredith.
她有一排假发，各种款式都有，特别是给梅雷迪思准备的。

376
00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:19.640
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

377
00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.860
Meredith was always having something done to her hair.
梅雷迪思的头发总是被折腾来折腾去。

378
00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:27.540
So, yeah, thank you so much, Kim, for the behind the scenes on that one.
所以，是的，非常感谢金分享了那一幕幕后的故事。

379
00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:33.820
So listen, and I know we're still talking about this opening scene, but I had to bring up something else.
听着，我知道我们还在讨论这个开场戏，但我必须提另一件事。

380
00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:34.460
What?
什么事？

381
00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:40.040
So when Michael walks through the door, he's carrying like nine gazillion bags, right?
当迈克尔走进门时，他提着大概几亿个袋子，对吧？

382
00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:46.340
And we're going to come to learn that one of them contains this steel drum that he has obsessed with playing.
我们后来会知道其中一个袋子里装着他沉迷演奏的钢鼓。

383
00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:47.840
He's holding a box.
他手里拿着一个盒子。

384
00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.900
He's holding bags and a box.
他手里拿着袋子和一个盒子。

385
00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.840
And the steel drum, I think, is in the box because it's a big rectangle.
我想钢鼓应该就在盒子里，因为那是个大长方形盒子。

386
00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:53.960
Same.
我也这么觉得。

387
00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:58.000
But it made me wonder what is in all the other bags.
但这让我好奇其他袋子里装的都是什么。

388
00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:01.900
And that is an amazing deleted scene.
那是一个很棒的删减片段。

389
00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:02.940
Yes, Jenna.
没错，珍娜。

390
00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.300
So those bags were gifts.
那些袋子里装的是礼物。

391
00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.760
They were like souvenirs that he bought everyone.
就像他给每个人买的纪念品一样。

392
00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:10.300
They definitely look like the souvenirs you bought at the airport.
它们看起来确实像是你在机场买的那种纪念品。

393
00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:12.300
And it's all in the deleted scenes.
这些都在删减片段里。

394
00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.240
He goes around the office handing them out.
他在办公室里到处分发这些礼物。

395
00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:20.760
Well, I remember doing that scene because the thing he gives Pam is a coconut bra.
我记得拍那场戏，因为他给帕姆的是一个椰子胸罩。

396
00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:24.480
And he's like, some coconuts for your coconuts.
他说：“给你的一对椰子，为了你的椰子。”

397
00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.820
And I'm like, thanks.
我说：“谢谢。”

398
00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:27.820
Then he says, do you want to see if it fits?
然后他说：“你想试试合不合适吗？”

399
00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.220
And you're like, no.
你当时肯定说：“不。”

400
00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:34.460
I'm not going to go try on this coconut bikini top right now.
我才不会现在就去试穿这个椰子比基尼上衣呢。

401
00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:35.020
Thanks.
谢谢。

402
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.380
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

403
00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:40.900
But I remember shooting that with Steve because I couldn't get through it.
但我记得和史蒂夫拍那场戏时，我总是演不下去。

404
00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:46.640
And every time I opened it up, it was so ludicrous to me that that was the gift he gave Pam.
每次我打开它，都觉得他送给帕姆的这份礼物太荒唐了。

405
00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.160
It would make me laugh.
这总让我忍不住笑场。

406
00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:52.460
He gives Angela Martin a lay and he puts it around her neck.
他给安吉拉·马丁戴上项链，然后套在她脖子上。

407
00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:53.520
And she's like, thank you.
她就说，谢谢你。

408
00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.140
And he goes, you just got laid.
然后他说，你刚被“上”了（lay）。

409
00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.460
And I'm like, no, I didn't.
我就说，不，我才没有。

410
00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.840
And you like rip it off, right?
然后你把它扯下来，对吧？

411
00:20:58.920 --> 00:20:59.840
Yeah, I get really mad.
对，我真的很生气。

412
00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:08.880
Well, next we're going to find out that Karen and Jim are experiencing some tension.
接下来我们要看到凯伦和吉姆之间出现了一些紧张气氛。

413
00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:10.060
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

414
00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.300
And here is why.
原因如下。

415
00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:18.360
It is because Jim does not want Karen to move into an apartment that is two blocks away from
因为吉姆不想让凯伦搬到离他公寓只有两个街区远的地方，

416
00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:22.940
his apartment, even though she's been having a really hard time finding an apartment and
尽管她一直很难找到住处，

417
00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:25.020
she is currently living in a motel.
而且目前还住在汽车旅馆里。

418
00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:27.700
She's at a day's end.
她已经走投无路了。

419
00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:29.800
That's what we learned that in a deleted scene.
这是我们在删减片段里了解到的。

420
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.020
I mean, come on.
我是说，拜托。

421
00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:35.000
Well, she says it down in the warehouse to Pam as well later.
好吧，她后来在仓库里也跟帕姆说了这件事。

422
00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:36.880
She needs to find a place to live.
她需要找个地方住。

423
00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:38.820
You know what I noticed?
你知道我注意到了什么吗？

424
00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:43.420
When Karen does her talking head, she's standing at the copier in the annex.
当凯伦做访谈时，她站在附楼的复印机旁。

425
00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:48.200
Remember in the other episode, we were like, is this copier always here?
还记得在另一集里，我们曾讨论过这台复印机是不是一直都在那儿吗？

426
00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:50.140
That's where she's standing.
她就站在那儿。

427
00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:54.580
That's backed by Kelly's desk and Toby's desk in the annex.
背后是附楼里凯莉和托比的办公桌。

428
00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:59.120
Jenna, what does it mean if your talking head is in the annex?
珍娜，如果访谈是在附楼拍的，那意味着什么？

429
00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:00.300
What does that mean?
那意味着什么？

430
00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:01.900
What does it mean?
到底意味着什么？

431
00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:06.240
I think it means you're trying to avoid somebody and you're using the copier in the annex.
我觉得这意味着你在试图躲避某人，所以才用附楼的复印机。

432
00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:07.100
Yeah.
没错。

433
00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:12.120
Jenna, speaking of deleted scenes, there's another great runner between Phyllis and Stanley.
珍娜，说到删减片段，菲利斯和斯坦利之间还有一段很棒的互动。

434
00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:16.160
Because, you know, Stanley says he doesn't get all of his bonus and he's not going to work.
因为你知道，斯坦利说他没拿到全部奖金，所以他拒绝工作。

435
00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.720
Not a lick until he gets that bonus money.
在拿到奖金之前，他什么都不会做。

436
00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:25.020
And it starts driving Phyllis crazy because he won't answer his phone.
这让菲利斯快疯了，因为他不接电话。

437
00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.460
She has a phenomenal talking head.
她有一段非常精彩的访谈。

438
00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:29.380
So that's in the DVD deleted scenes.
那段内容在DVD的删减片段里。

439
00:22:30.380 --> 00:22:33.060
